Phosphofructokinase-1 (option A) is a key glycolytic enzyme and is inhibited during fasting, and hydroxymethylglutaryl-CoA lyase (option D) plays a role in ketogenesis. In contrast, phosphoenolpyruvate carboxykinase (option B) is one of the major rate‐limiting enzymes in gluconeogenesis, converting oxaloacetate to phosphoenolpyruvate. Thus, option B most contributes to maintaining normal serum glucose levels in this fasting patient.

